⬇️FULL RECIPE⬇️
322 calories 33g protein (for the entire pint, toppings/mix-ins included)

Royal @Reeses Fluffernutter Protein @Dairy Queen Blizzard 😋🍦

Original recipe from my Recipe Book

Check out the link in my bio for my Creami Recipe Books with over 135 recipes like this one!

- 1 Vanilla Protein Shake (11oz - I like the ones from @Nurri)
- 20-25g @Lakanto Monk Fruit sweetener
- 2.5g (½ tsp) vanilla bean paste (or extract)
- 1g (¼ tsp) salt
- 1g (¼ tsp) xanthan gum
Mix-ins/Toppings:
- 11g Reese’s PB Cups, chopped into small pieces
- 18g (3 tbsp) marshmallow creme (same thing as Marshmallow fluff)
- 10g peanut butter chips + 1.5g coconut oil + a pinch of salt
• Right before the Mix-In cycle, combine the peanut butter chips, coconut oil, and salt, and melt in the microwave (30 sec intervals, stirring in between). Then, hollow out a hole in the center of the base, and pour in. After spinning on the Mix-In setting, it’ll turn into a beautiful peanut butter swirl!
322 cal 27g C, 11g F, 33g P

Instructions:
1. Blend all ingredients for the base and freeze (at least 16 hours)
2. Run your pint under hot water for at least 60 seconds
3. Spin on “Lite Ice Cream” setting
4. Spin on “Respin” setting (if powdery)
5. Make a hole down to the bottom with a butter knife and fill with the chopped PB cups and melted PB chip mixture
6. Run the “Mix-in” cycle
7. Make a hole down to the bottom with a butter knife (if there isn’t one already - there should already be one because we aren’t using a full pint’s worth of liquid) and fill with the marshmallow creme

